  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 945 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nA dry cold frontal passage will bring an increase in cloud cover \novernight. Behind the front winds will become northwesterly for \nSunday, and with a tightening pressure gradient and deeper mixing up \nto around 850mb gusts will increase to around 25-35 mph Sunday \nafternoon, strongest across northern WI, before subsiding Sunday \nevening.\n\nA brief period of high pressure Monday will keep the forecast dry \nand temps a few degrees above normal before the next frontal passage \ncomes Tuesday into Wednesday. NBM probs continue to show 20 to 30% \nPoPs, highest over the over the lake effect belts of north-central \nWI as well as northern Door Co. Colder shot of air also arrives \nduring this time as 850 mb temps fall to -7 to -9C, hinting at the \npotential for snow flurries mixing in with light rain at times.\nOtherwise, respectable signal (50 to 60%) exists for below normal \nprecipitation and above normal temperatures into the middle of the \nNovember.",
